    ("MY", "Politics", FARAH,
     "Sabah fishing villages given a say in coastal development plans",
     "A new rule requires consultation with villages before reclamation or resort projects are approved.",
     [
         "Coastal villages in Sabah will have to be consulted before reclamation, resort or port projects near them are approved, under rules passed by the state assembly in September after protests over a resort planned near Kota Belud.",
         "Developers must now hold at least 2 public meetings in the affected village and publish an assessment of the project's effect on fishing grounds and mangroves, in Malay and in the local language where needed.",
         "## Why the change",
         "Fishing communities along Sabah's west coast say reclamation and resort construction have destroyed mangroves and reefs where they fish and collect shellfish. In several cases, villagers learnt of projects only when bulldozers arrived.",
         "“We found out from the machines,” said a fisherman from a village near Tuaran whose family has fished the same bay for 4 generations. “Nobody asked us anything.”",
         "## What the rules require",
         "Projects affecting more than 5 hectares of coast or mangrove need an independent study of fish stocks before approval. Villages can submit written objections, which the planning committee must answer.",
         "## Limits",
         "The rules do not give villages a veto. Environmental groups said they were a step forward but feared that meetings would become a box-ticking exercise.",
         "Developers' associations welcomed clearer procedures but warned that long consultations could delay investment in a state that needs jobs. The state government said the first projects under the new rules, a jetty in Semporna and a hotel expansion near Kudat, would be assessed before the end of the year.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Business", FARAH,
     "Pahang durian growers ship frozen whole fruit to China",
     "Exports have surged since whole frozen durians were allowed into the Chinese market.",
     [
         "Durian growers in Pahang are shipping record volumes of frozen whole durians to China, after Chinese authorities allowed imports of whole frozen fruit from Malaysia in 2024. Previously only pulp and paste could be exported.",
         "Exports of frozen whole durians reached about 18,000 tonnes in the first 8 months of this year, more than double the same period last year, according to industry figures.",
         "## Musang King leads",
         "Most exports are of the Musang King variety, prized in China for its rich, bitter-sweet flesh. A single fruit can sell for the equivalent of RM150 or more in Shanghai.",
         "“Ten years ago we sold everything at the roadside,” said a grower in Raub who has 400 trees. “Now buyers from Guangzhou come to the farm in June and pay before the fruit falls.”",
         "## Freezing the king",
         "Durians are frozen whole within hours of falling, at about -80°C, which preserves the flavour. Several new freezing plants have opened near Raub and Bentong.",
         "## Risks and land",
         "The boom has encouraged growers to clear more land for orchards. Environmental groups in Pahang say some new plantations have been cut into forest reserves and steep hillsides, raising the risk of landslides and polluting rivers with soil.",
         "Thailand and Vietnam also export durians to China, and prices could fall if supply rises faster than demand. Economists advised growers not to borrow heavily on the assumption that prices stay high, noting that the Thai durian boom saw prices fall by about 30% in a single season when harvests overlapped.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Technology", FARAH,
     "Rural Sarawak schools add coding classes taught over satellite links",
     "Pupils in longhouse communities learn programming with teachers based in Kuching.",
     [
         "Primary schools in rural Sarawak have begun teaching coding to pupils aged 10 to 12, with lessons delivered by teachers in Kuching over satellite internet links installed in the past 2 years.",
         "The programme now reaches 64 schools, many in longhouse communities upriver that can only be reached by boat or logging road.",
         "## How lessons work",
         "Pupils use tablets and simple block-based programming tools to build games and animations. A teacher in Kuching leads the lesson on a screen, while a local teacher helps in the classroom.",
         "“The first time a girl made a character jump on screen, the whole class shouted,” said a teacher at a school near Kapit. “Some of these children had never used a computer before this year.”",
         "Lessons are in Malay and English, and teachers mix in Iban words for younger pupils. Each school gets a set of 20 tablets, charged from the same solar panels that run the satellite dish.",
         "## Connectivity",
         "Until recently, many of the schools had no internet at all. The state has funded satellite dishes and solar panels for 220 rural schools since 2023.",
         "On cloudy days the connection drops, and teachers keep offline lessons ready on the tablets.",
         "## Next steps",
         "Organisers want to train local teachers to run the lessons themselves, so the programme does not depend on Kuching. About 90 teachers have completed a 6-week course.",
         "Parents said they hoped the skills would give children options beyond plantation work. Some older pupils have begun helping their families use phones to sell crafts and pepper online, a small sign, teachers said, of what the lessons could open up.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Science", FARAH,
     "Drones help count sea turtle nests on Terengganu beaches",
     "Night-time thermal cameras spot nesting turtles without disturbing them.",
     [
         "Researchers in Terengganu are using drones with thermal cameras to count sea turtles coming ashore to nest, an approach that lets them survey kilometres of beach at night without disturbing the animals.",
         "Green and hawksbill turtles nest on beaches along the Terengganu coast between April and September. The state's leatherback turtles, once famous at Rantau Abang, have almost disappeared, with only a handful of nests recorded in recent decades.",
         "## How it works",
         "Turtles show up clearly in thermal images against cooler sand. A drone flying at about 50 metres can cover a 10-kilometre beach in under an hour, compared with a full night for a team walking the beach.",
         "In a trial on Redang Island, the drones recorded 212 nesting attempts over 3 weeks, closely matching counts by rangers on foot.",
         "“Every time we walk past a turtle with a torch, we risk scaring her back into the sea,” said a marine biologist at a university in Kuala Terengganu. “The drone stays high and silent.”",
         "## Protecting eggs",
         "Rangers collect many eggs and move them to protected hatcheries, where they are safe from poachers and predators. Since 2022, selling turtle eggs has been banned throughout Terengganu.",
         "## Temperature and sex",
         "Sand temperature determines whether hatchlings are male or female, with warmer nests producing more females. Researchers are using sensors to check whether hatcheries are getting too warm, and have begun shading some nests with netting.",
         "The data will help decide which beaches to protect from development.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Health", FARAH,
     "Dengue cases fall in Selangor neighbourhoods after mosquito releases",
     "Mosquitoes carrying Wolbachia bacteria reduce the virus's spread.",
     [
         "Dengue cases have fallen sharply in Selangor neighbourhoods where mosquitoes carrying Wolbachia bacteria have been released, health officials say, with some areas recording up to 75% fewer cases than similar areas without releases.",
         "Wolbachia, a bacterium found naturally in many insects, makes it harder for Aedes mosquitoes to transmit the dengue virus. Once released, the mosquitoes breed and spread the bacterium through the local population.",
         "## A heavy burden",
         "Malaysia recorded more than 120,000 dengue cases in 2023, with Selangor accounting for about half. The disease causes fever and severe pain, and can be fatal in a small share of cases.",
         "“Before, every few months someone in our block had dengue,” said a resident of Shah Alam whose son was hospitalised in 2022. “This year, nobody I know has had it.”",
         "## How releases work",
         "Health workers release mosquitoes weekly for several months in each neighbourhood, using small containers left in gardens and drains.",
         "Residents are told in advance through community leaders and mosques. The released mosquitoes bite like ordinary ones, which worried some residents at first.",
         "In Taman Sri Muda, one of the first areas covered, cases fell from 196 in 2021 to 31 last year. The hospital in Klang reported fewer dengue admissions in the same period.",
         "## Still important",
         "Officials stressed that Wolbachia did not replace clearing breeding sites. Water collecting in pots, tyres and blocked gutters still needs to be emptied every week.",
         "The programme now covers about 40 localities in Selangor and Kuala Lumpur. Officials plan to expand it to Johor and Penang, where dengue rates have also risen, by 2027.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Environment", FARAH,
     "Cameron Highlands farmers terrace slopes to stop landslides",
     "Vegetable farms on steep hillsides are adding terraces, drains and grass strips.",
     [
         "Vegetable farmers in the Cameron Highlands are building terraces and drains on steep slopes, in a programme to reduce landslides and the mud that pours into rivers after heavy rain.",
         "The highlands, about 1,500 metres above sea level in Pahang, grow much of Malaysia's cabbage, tomatoes and lettuce. Many farms were cut into hillsides with little protection against erosion.",
         "## Muddy rivers",
         "After storms, rivers running from the highlands turn brown with soil. Mud has filled reservoirs downstream, and landslides have blocked roads and destroyed farms. In 2014, a flood of mud and water killed several people in Bertam Valley.",
         "“We lost a whole field of cabbages in one night last year,” said a farmer near Kampung Raja. “The slope just slid into the valley.”",
         "## What is changing",
         "Under the programme, farmers receive grants to build terraces, line drains with concrete and plant vetiver grass along slope edges. The deep-rooted grass holds soil in place.",
         "About 300 farms have joined since 2023.",
         "## Land and permits",
         "Many farms in the Cameron Highlands operate on land without formal titles, which has made enforcement of farming rules difficult. The state government has offered temporary licences to farmers who agree to adopt soil protection measures.",
         "Environmental groups said terracing helped but that some of the steepest slopes should not be farmed at all. Water quality monitoring by the state shows sediment levels in the Bertam River fell by about a fifth in the first 2 years, after the programme's first terraces were finished.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Sport", FARAH,
     "Sepak takraw leagues draw young crowds in Kelantan",
     "Weekend matches fill community halls as the sport gets a new generation of fans.",
     [
         "Sepak takraw, the acrobatic game in which players kick a rattan or plastic ball over a net, is drawing young crowds to weekend leagues in Kelantan, with matches filling community halls and attracting thousands of viewers online.",
         "A new state league with 16 teams started this year, streaming every match free on social media.",
         "## The game",
         "Teams of 3 players use their feet, knees, chest and head to send the ball over a net about 1.5 metres high. The most spectacular move is the overhead spike, a scissor kick that can send the ball down at more than 100 kilometres an hour.",
         "“The first time I saw a roll spike in real life, I could not believe a person could do that,” said a 14-year-old from Kota Bharu who now trains 4 evenings a week.",
         "## Roots in the region",
         "Sepak takraw has been played in Malaysia, Thailand, Indonesia and neighbouring countries for centuries, originally as a game of keeping the ball in the air in a circle. Malaysia has won several regional titles, but Thailand has dominated the sport internationally.",
         "## Streaming helps",
         "Organisers said live streams had brought in sponsors, including local food companies and phone shops. The best matches have drawn more than 50,000 viewers online.",
         "Kelantan's state sports council plans to build an indoor court with seating for 1,500 people in Kota Bharu. Coaches hope a stronger league will help Malaysia challenge Thailand at the next Southeast Asian Games, where the Malaysian men's team took silver in 2023.",
     ]),
    ("MY", "Health", FARAH,
     "Boat clinics bring doctors to river villages in Sarawak",
     "A floating clinic visits longhouses along the Rajang River every month.",
     [
         "A clinic built on a river boat now visits 38 longhouse communities along the Rajang River in Sarawak every month, bringing doctors, nurses and medicines to villages hours from the nearest hospital.",
         "The 20-metre boat has 2 consultation rooms, a small pharmacy, a dental chair and equipment for basic blood tests and ultrasound scans.",
         "## Why a boat",
         "Many communities upriver from Kapit and Belaga have no road access. Reaching the hospital in Sibu can take a full day by express boat and costs more than many families earn in a week.",
         "“My mother is 81 and cannot travel,” said a resident of a longhouse near Belaga. “The boat comes to the jetty below our house. The doctor even climbs up to see her.”",
         "## What they treat",
         "Most patients have high blood pressure, diabetes, skin infections or dental problems. The team also vaccinates children and checks pregnant women.",
         "Over 12 months, the boat recorded about 9,000 consultations. Serious cases are referred to Kapit or Sibu, and the team arranges transport.",
         "## Water levels",
         "In the dry season, low water levels and logs in the river can stop the boat reaching the furthest villages. The team then switches to a smaller longboat, carrying only medicines and a nurse.",
         "The state health department plans a second boat for the Baram River in 2027. Staff turnover is a problem, as postings involve weeks away from family, and the department has raised allowances for doctors and nurses who join.",
     ]),
